Here's a simple implementation of a text-based adventure game in Python. This game has only one location (a dark forest) and a limited set of actions (go north, go south, go east, go west, look, take, drop). You can extend this game by adding more locations, objects, and actions.

```python
def print_welcome():
    print("Welcome to the Dark Forest Adventure Game!")

def get_user_input():
    while True:
        user_input = input("Enter a command (go north/south/east/west, look, take, drop, or quit): ").lower()
        if user_input == "quit":
            return "quit"
        elif user_input in ["north", "south", "east", "west"]:
            return user_input
        elif user_input in ["look", "examine"]:
            return "look"
        elif user_input in ["take", "grab"]:
            return "take"
        elif user_input in ["drop", "put"]:
            return "drop"
        else:
            print("Invalid command. Please try again.")

def process_user_input(user_input):
    if user_input == "quit":
        return None
    elif user_input == "look":
        print("You are in a dark forest.")
    elif user_input == "take":
        print("You cannot take anything in this location.")
    elif user_input == "drop":
        print("You cannot drop anything in this location.")
    else:
        direction = user_input[3:]  # Remove 'go' from the command
        if direction == "north":
            print("You are now in a clearing.")
        elif direction == "south":
            print("You are now in a cave.")
        elif direction == "east":
            print("You are now in a dense forest.")
        elif direction == "west":
            print("You are now in a rocky path.")
        else:
            print("Invalid direction. Please try again.")

def main():
    print_welcome()
    while True:
        user_input = get_user_input()
        if user_input is None:
            break
        process_user_input(user_input)

if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
```

This program will create a simple text-based adventure game for you to explore. You can extend this game by adding more locations, objects, and actions.
